  "description": "EGEZAS crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 2 d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H97 Er4 N51 O39 4+,8(Br1 1-),4(H3 O1 1+),23(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1D (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2D (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.564-3.779 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.74-108.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (H3O)4[Er4(OH)5(H2O)4(μ2-IN)(IN@CB[6])2]Br8·23H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
